# Drafted by Gemini (R11 batch b1), edited. doris_squire's first conversation.

~ start
set doris_squire_met
Narrator: Iron keys clink at her belt, and she smells of cold tallow and scrubbed stone.
doris_squire [neutral]: Strangers. Keep your blades sheathed in the Round and we will get on fine.
* Ask about the law in Wickermoor -> about_work
* Ask about the village -> about_village
* Ask about the law and the jail -> shop_open
* Ask about the oak in the square -> rumour
* [Perception DC 14] Glance at the small paper tucked under her blotter -> secret_ok | secret_fail
* Report a suspicion about someone -> accuse_start
* Take our leave -> END

~ about_work
doris_squire [neutral]: Three cells behind me. Fines for brawling, banishment for grand theft, and for murder the Mayor takes your head before the Oak of Many Faces.
-> menu

~ about_village
doris_squire [weary]: Good folk mostly, when not spooked by moor-fog or preaching in the mud. Finish your business before the late bells and stick to the lantern paths.
-> menu

~ shop_open
doris_squire [neutral]: If you want honest coin, there is the bounty board.
-> menu

~ rumour
doris_squire [neutral]: Every face in that bark was on the parish roll once. After a sentence, the roots drink deep and the moss stays red for a week.
-> menu

~ secret_ok
Narrator: Beneath a brass sunflower weight lies a scrap of neat verse about rain on quiet wheat.
doris_squire [angry]: Eyes on my face, traveler. A woman is allowed a bit of quiet ink between lockups.
-> menu

~ secret_fail
Narrator: Her broad hand covers the blotter like a slate slab dropping into place.
doris_squire [neutral]: Charge sheets are for the watch, not for tourists.
-> menu

~ menu
* Ask about the law in Wickermoor -> about_work
* Ask about the village -> about_village
* Ask about the law and the jail -> shop_open
* Ask about the oak in the square -> rumour
* [Perception DC 14] Glance at the small paper tucked under her blotter -> secret_ok | secret_fail
* Report a suspicion about someone -> accuse_start
* Take our leave -> END

~ accuse_start
doris_squire [neutral]: Name.
* Alda Farnum, the innkeeper -> accuse_alda
* Randall Graham, the barber -> accuse_randall
* Baltus Tolliver, the merchant -> accuse_baltus
* Howie Butterman, your deputy -> accuse_howie
* Theodora Mayville, the postmaster -> accuse_theodora
* Gaston Doray, the painter -> accuse_gaston
* Never mind -> menu

~ accuse_alda
if flag.cult_clue_alda_farnum and flag.cult_proof_alda
doris_squire [neutral]: Hares. A ledger. I will watch her.
set accused_alda
else
doris_squire [neutral]: Not enough. Bring more.
endif
-> accuse_start

~ accuse_randall
if flag.cult_clue_randall_graham and flag.cult_proof_randall
doris_squire [neutral]: A carved hare. Swept hair. I will watch him.
set accused_randall
else
doris_squire [neutral]: Not enough. Bring more.
endif
-> accuse_start

~ accuse_baltus
if flag.cult_clue_baltus_tolliver and flag.cult_proof_baltus
doris_squire [neutral]: A ring. A pipe. I will watch him.
set accused_baltus
else
doris_squire [neutral]: Not enough. Bring more.
endif
-> accuse_start

~ accuse_howie
if flag.cult_clue_howie_butterman and flag.cult_proof_howie
doris_squire [neutral]: My own. Hmph. I will watch him.
set accused_howie
else
doris_squire [neutral]: Not enough. Bring more.
endif
-> accuse_start

~ accuse_gaston
if flag.cult_clue_gaston_doray and flag.cult_proof_gaston
doris_squire [neutral]: Hares in every painting. A boy with no past. I will watch him.
set accused_gaston
else
doris_squire [neutral]: Not enough. Bring more.
endif
-> accuse_start

~ accuse_theodora
doris_squire [neutral]: The postmaster is the post. Bring more than that, and mind what you say of her.
-> accuse_start
